{"term":"continent","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:78222c3b1edd22ac40","definition":"One of the main contiguous landmasses, separated by water or geological features, on the surface of a planet, sometimes including its continental shelves and the islands on them.","example":"But I should turn mine ears and hear\nThe moanings of the homeless sea,\n⁠The sound of streams that swift or slow\n⁠Draw down Æonian hills, and sow\nThe dust of continents to be; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["archicontinent","continental","continentlike","continent of stability","continentwide","coontinent","cuntinent","microcontinent","midcontinent","palaeocontinent","paleocontinent","protocontinent","pseudocontinent","subcontinent","supercontinent","the Continent","ur-continent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ae80e7b3124ebe4608","definition":"Each of the traditional main regions into which the Earth’s land surface is divided, including both an extent of mainland and various conventionally associated islands, etc; namely, Africa, Europe, Asia, Australasia/Oceania, North America, South America, and Antarctica.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["archicontinent","continental","continentlike","continent of stability","continentwide","coontinent","cuntinent","microcontinent","midcontinent","palaeocontinent","paleocontinent","protocontinent","pseudocontinent","subcontinent","supercontinent","the Continent","ur-continent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6a81c1dedd6bc6032d","definition":"A large contiguous landmass as opposed to its islands, peninsulas, and so forth; mainland. Also specifically, the Old World continent of Europe–Asia–Africa: see the Continent.","example":"No man is an Iland, intire of it ſelfe; euery man is a peece of the Continent, a part of the maine; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, obsolete","register":"broadly, obsolete","wordFamily":["archicontinent","continental","continentlike","continent of stability","continentwide","coontinent","cuntinent","microcontinent","midcontinent","palaeocontinent","paleocontinent","protocontinent","pseudocontinent","subcontinent","supercontinent","the Continent","ur-continent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7dcae1db3a9a557a9","definition":"A large connected expanse of something in general.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["archicontinent","continental","continentlike","continent of stability","continentwide","coontinent","cuntinent","microcontinent","midcontinent","palaeocontinent","paleocontinent","protocontinent","pseudocontinent","subcontinent","supercontinent","the Continent","ur-continent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c3ae866ff7700aa493","definition":"Any continuous tract or area of land; country, connected region.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["archicontinent","continental","continentlike","continent of stability","continentwide","coontinent","cuntinent","microcontinent","midcontinent","palaeocontinent","paleocontinent","protocontinent","pseudocontinent","subcontin